   whatwrong="In `routes/metering.ts` the handler of `GET /usage` (line 108) awaits `getUsageSummary(reqTenantId(req), from, to)` and, in its catch (line 128), logs `logger.error('Failed to read metering usage', { error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error) });` (line 129) and then answers the CONSTANT 500 `{ success: false, error: { code: 'INTERNAL_ERROR', message: 'Failed to read usage' } }`. If the query rejects with a revoked Proxy, `error instanceof Error` itself throws a TypeError inside the catch; if it rejects with an Error whose `message` getter throws, `error.message` throws. Either way the catch throws before anything is logged and before the 500 is sent; the async handler rejects, Express 4 does not catch that, and the request gets no response. The fix keeps the `logger.error` line's text and replaces only the value: it first reads the same expression into a local `reason` inside its own `try`, and a `catch` sets the constant `'unreadable thrown value'`; the log line then uses `{ error: reason }`. This is the inline guard already merged in originate `routes/certifications.ts` (`let reason`, around line 1087); this file has no helper and none is added. The `res.status(500).json(...)` lines are NOT touched.",
   callers="CALLERS (git grep at the tip): `meteringRouter` is the partner-facing, tenant-scoped read API mounted by `src/index.ts`; `GET /usage` has no in-repo caller (partners / Platform S call it over HTTP through the gateway). **Billing-input check:** the handler is READ-ONLY. It calls only `getUsageSummary` (chargeEvents.ts :261), one SELECT over `charge_events` (`COUNT`, `SUM`, `GROUP BY`, no INSERT/UPDATE); the route file contains no write and no other catch. The catch runs after the read has failed, so no recorded usage count (the billing input in `charge_events`) is created, changed or skipped by this patch in any case. **BEHAVIOUR CHANGE the raise PR must state:** for an unreadable thrown value only, today the catch throws, nothing is logged and the partner gets NO answer (hung request); after, the constant reason is logged and the partner gets the constant 500 `Failed to read usage` that an ordinary Error already gets (response body identical for every value). Persisted state: none.",
